{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"ac3ed2db92437819fe519de46f48be51c1cab0ffee871693a0800a9c502828a3","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar config validate command","key_entities":["rebar config validate","src/rebar/_commands/show_config.py::_validate","src/rebar/_config_sections.py","reconciler.rich_text_cutover","_raw_toml_tables","load_config","scan_tombstones","TICKETS_TRACKER_DIR","_SECTIONS","mcp.http_port"],"problem_keywords":["config validation","enum constraint","typed coercion","tombstone scanning","invalid configuration"],"propositions":["rebar config validate bypasses typed coercion and enum validation by calling only scan_tombstones over raw TOML, allowing invalid enum values like reconciler.rich_text_cutover=\"clould\" to pass with exit 0.","The command should aggregate both tombstone diagnostics and typed-value validation errors in a single run and exit non-zero when invalid configuration is detected.","Invalid enum and non-enum typed values on live keys (reconciler.rich_text_cutover, mcp.http_port) are correctly rejected by rebar config but not validated by rebar config validate.","Validation must enumerate and coerce all registered typed keys through the canonical _SECTIONS path while preserving the same-run tombstone report without early exit or store mounting."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787317518897279001,"uuid":"087c06b1-478f-4ba2-adb9-6a5b9d64e482"}